# Cloudflare Pages Redirects
#
# Static assets that do not exist must say so with a 404 — never the SPA
# shell at 200. During a deploy window the shell-as-200 answer was cached
# under the stylesheet's URL (browsers honour the year-long immutable
# header, and the service worker trusts response.ok), and the store then
# served HTML as its CSS: a completely unstyled page. Existing files are
# served before these rules run, so the 404 line only fires for assets
# that genuinely do not exist.
/static/* /index.html 404

# All other routes serve index.html for client-side routing
/* /index.html 200
